THE NAME IS NOT PART OF THE GRANT.

Apache-2.0 section 6 withholds trademark rights, and that is deliberate here
rather than incidental. "Ame" and "Mētis", and the logo artwork, are marks
identifying this author's work. The licence lets you fork the system, take the
tokens, adapt the gate and ship what you build — it does not let you call the
result Ame. Rename your fork.

This is the whole reason the project moved from MIT to Apache-2.0. MIT is
silent on names, so under it a fork could carry the name of the thing it forked
and a reader could not tell them apart. The permission to reuse the work was
never the problem; the ambiguity about whose work it is was.

